we are all pretty sad that attack on  titan is ending soon but don't worry we  got you covered because in today's video  we'll be covering top 12 animes similar  to attack on titan number 12. black  bullet  black bullet shares more than just a  post-apocalyptic setting with attack on  titan it also has characters that feel  like they will never escape their  circumstances as well as many similar  plot devices and themes this anime is  about a post-apocalyptic japan where  most of the humans have been infected  with the gastria virus and turned into  monsters what is left of mankind now  lives within the monolith walls sounds  familiar right to combat this threat  people are trained to become weapons  known as promoters or civil officers  these promoters work in teams with the  initiators young girls with superhuman  abilities black bullet revolves around  the team of venju an initiator and  rentaro a promoter as they go on  missions to fight the growing threat of  gastria in their hometown of tokyo  number 11. fate apocrypha  fate apocrypha is a unique take on the  fate series instead of the usual battle  royale among seven mages it features two  teams of seven masters and their  servants fighting against each other in  order to obtain something called the  holy grail the only problem none of them  know what exactly it does just like an  attack on titan these characters are not  your typical heroes either which makes  things all that more compelling as you  watch them fight to try and achieve  their goals there are many mysteries  within both anime shows that keep the  viewers interested until the very end  number 10. claymore  you unwittingly led me right to your own  death  claymore is set in the world where the  shape-shifting demons known as yoma eat  humans one of these monsters arrives in  rocky's village and kills his family but  before it can kill rocky a claymore  claire appears and saves him the  claymores are half human half yoma  hybrid warriors with the express purpose  of exterminating these monsters the  story then follows rocky and claire as  they travel from down to town defeating  yomas along the way both claymore and  attack on titan are very similar both  are set in medieval times where humans  are fighting against man-eating monsters  also both are quite violent and make use  of swords and combat if you are a fan of  aot this is surely the anime for you  number nine blue exorcist you are not a  human being rin  you are the son of a demon born by a  human blue exorcist follows rin okumara  who appears to be an ordinary teenager  but his world is turned upside down when  he finds out that he is the son of an  actual satan not wanting to join his  father he starts his training in order  to become an exorcist the similarities  between attack on titan and blue  exorcist can be found literally  everywhere we will only mention a few to  avoid spoilers both protagonists are 15  year old boys both of them discover that  they have similar powers to the enemy  they are fighting and their enemies have  been a threat to humanity since forever  both characters aaron and ren also have  the same voice actor in the english  version we can all agree that nothing  can beat attack on titan but you should  give blue exorcist a try it may surprise  you number eight elfin lead  okay i will be honest with you guys  elfin lead doesn't really have that much  in common with attack on titan but it's  an exceptional anime and we are sure  that a lot of aot fans will find it  entertaining lucy is a special breed of  human referred to as declonius born with  a short pair of horns and invisible  telekinetic hands she was severely  abused by human beings and subsequently  wants to murder them all as revenge  elfin lead involves some heavy themes  like revenge jealousy regret and the  value of humanity this anime is  certainly not everyone's cup of tea but  if you've liked what you've heard so far  definitely go and check it out number  seven full metal alchemist brotherhood  [Music]  in order for something to be obtained  something of equal value must be lost  this is the main rule of alchemy and  full metal alchemist brotherhood this  anime is about two brothers edward and  al who are talented state alchemists  that have lost their body parts due to a  failed attempt at human transmutation  three years of searching later the  brothers seek the philosopher's stone a  mythical relic that allows an alchemist  to overcome the law of equivalent  exchange attack on titan is very similar  in terms of how it handles its  characters and both shows are full of  death and unexpected plot twists it is  one of the best rated anime shows ever  so what are you waiting for go and watch  it number six serif of the end the only  reason i'm here is to get revenge on  those blood sucking freaks with the  appearance of a mysterious virus that  kills everyone above the age of 13 power  hungry vampires emerge in order to  subjugate society  because of that young children are now  at their mercy with some becoming  blood-sucking creatures themselves  yuichiro is the only one who is able to  escape his fate he later joins the  imperial demon army a military unit  tasked with killing all vampires in  japan alongside other characters the  group has to figure out how they're  going to defeat this new threat number 5  god eater  [Music]  this anime is about a world where  creatures known as origami are taking  over the planet on top of that people  also have to worry about getting eaten  by them the only ones who can fight  against these monsters are the god  eaters humans who have been found to be  compatible with one of the living  origami weapons made to harm and devour  other origami attack on titan and god  ear both show off very similar themes  there's always an impending doom be it  titans or origami that makes things all  the more suspenseful once you start  watching god eater is not interesting  just because it shares similarities with  aot but also due to how many characters  within the show aren't typical heroes  which brings something fresh to your  usual action-packed anime number 4.  helsing ultimate  if you're a fan of attack on titan  helsing ultimate is one of the animes  that you'll definitely enjoy watching  instead of fighting titans the heroes  within this anime are hunting down  different types of creatures including  werewolves and zombies none of which can  be easily defeated it's about an  organization known as helsing that  utilizes its own vampire alucard to  fight against other creatures alucard is  a ruthless and ridiculously strong  vampire that fights his own kind along  with everything else who tries to oppose  helsing other than monsters trying to  destroy humanity this anime doesn't  share that much with attack on titan but  still we urge you to go and watch it you  won't be disappointed number three  castlevania pack and go  and do not look back  castlevania is actually an american  anime based on a series of japanese  video games with the same name the anime  features trevor belmont as the main  protagonist on a quest to stop the evil  dracula who seeks to destroy humanity  following the execution of his wife lisa  castlevania is the first ever video game  adaptation to get a very good score and  ratings from various critics it may not  sound compelling at first glance but  castlevania does have some great action  scenes which makes it worth watching  number 2 tokyo ghoul  ken kaneki is a boy who goes on a date  with rize a girl he met in cafe however  rize is not exactly who she seems she is  actually a monster that eats people a  ghoul kaneki soon becomes a half ghoul  and he is dragged into a conflict with  many others like him he is forced to  live in two worlds one where he is seen  as monsters and another where he is  considered human attack on titan has a  lot of similar themes when it comes to  its characters both animes are set in a  cruel world and the main characters are  forced to find a way to survive number  1. kabaneri of the iron fortress  out of all the animes on this list this  one is by far the most similar to attack  on titan horrific creatures emerge from  a mysterious virus ripping through the  flesh of humans to save their  never-ending appetite to combat this  people have built fortresses around  their cities in order to protect them  from these monsters wow that sounds  familiar but on top of that the anime is  actually made by the same studio that  made the first three seasons of attack  on titan and we can all agree that  attack on titan looks amazing well i  don't think i need to persuade you  anymore close this video and go watch  kabaneri right now but before you leave  hitting a like button would be great and  you can also subscribe for more anime  content like this okay you can leave now  bye

